===Future licence plate design===

In October 2025, the provincial government announced an online vote for the choice of a new license plate design would be held. All 8 choices have replaced "Wild Rose Country" with "Strong and Free", taken from ''Fortis et Libre'' ([[Latin]]) on the Alberta Coat of Arms, which in turn is from the Canadian national anthem. The new license plate will feature the Moraine Lake and will start being issued in mid 2026 likely starting with the sequence DBB-0000 continuing the current ABC-1234 format in use since the early 2010s skipping vowels and the letter Q, the current 1983 base will still continue to be valid. <ref>{{Cite web |last=Alberta |first=Government of |date=2025-11-18 |title=The results are in: new plate revealed {{!}} Nous avons les résultats : la province dévoile une nouvelle plaque d’immatriculation |url=https://www.alberta.ca/news.aspx |access-date=2025-11-23 |website=www.alberta.ca |language=en-CA}}</ref> 

